// PostToolUse hook: record WHICH CONVERSATION filed an ask (mt#3564).
//
// The write half of the answered-ask injection. This hook exists for the same reason
// `stamp-session-creator-link.ts` (mt#3120) does — it is the only place that sees both
// ids at once. The harness hands it the conversation uuid as `input.session_id`, and
// the newly-minted ask id comes back in the tool's own result. Neither is available to
// `asks.create` itself: the MCP transport does not carry a conversation id, which is
// why `Ask.parentSessionId` is caller-supplied and empty on essentially every ask.
//
// ## Why the result is readable at all (mt#3182 -> mt#3308)
//
// This hook's precedent shipped BROKEN and stayed green: `stamp-session-creator-link.ts`
// wrote ZERO rows against 235 sessions because it read `tool_result`, and production's
// PostToolUse payload carries `tool_response`. Its unit tests hand-built a `tool_result`
// and so exercised a payload production never produces.
//
// mt#3308 fixed the root cause in `types.ts`: `normalizeToolResult` unwraps production's
// MCP content envelope (`[{type:"text", text:"<json>"}]`) onto the `tool_result` key.
// `readInput` applies it, so reading `tool_result` here is correct AGAINST PRODUCTION —
// but the lesson stands, and this hook's test suite asserts against the ENVELOPE shape
// (`tool_response`), not a hand-built `tool_result`, so a regression in that
// normalization fails this hook's tests rather than silently disabling it.
//
// Unlike its precedent this hook has no fallback: `asks.create` MINTS the id in its
// result, so there is no `tool_input` field to recover it from. A create whose result
// cannot be parsed is simply not attributed — no notice for that ask, no other harm.
//
// ## Why no database
//
// See `ask-conversation-map.ts`'s header. Short version: a DB-writing hook needs
// `reflect-metadata` and initialized configuration and fails differently at each layer
// (mem#672), and the eventual consumer reads a local file regardless (ADR-028 D7(5)).
//
// Fail-open and silent by construction: every failure path exits 0. A missed stamp
// costs one undelivered notice; it must never fail the `asks_create` call itself.
//
